%% Storefront analytics and privacy-safe purchase activity
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Browser
    participant Web as Customer Web/BFF
    participant Analytics as Analytics API
    participant Sanitize as Event sanitizer
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Report as Bounded aggregate service
    participant Activity as Purchase activity API
    participant Settings as Tenant settings

    Browser->>Web: View product, search, filter, cart, or checkout
    Web->>Web: Create anonymous/session event identity
    Web->>Analytics: POST event with bounded metadata
    Analytics->>Sanitize: Normalize path, filters, and search terms
    Sanitize->>Sanitize: Remove unsafe scalar/PII-like values
    Sanitize->>DB: Persist tenant-local structured event

    opt Admin analytics dashboard
        Web->>Report: Request bounded date/filter aggregation
        Report->>DB: Aggregate daily/event facts in tenant DB
        DB-->>Report: Measured funnel and revenue/order totals
        Report-->>Web: Tenant-scoped dashboard projection
    end

    opt Public purchase activity
        Browser->>Web: Request page of recent activity
        Web->>Activity: Forward tenant-scoped activity request
        Activity->>Settings: Check activity enabled and policy
        Activity->>DB: Select delivered/completed opted-in orders
        DB-->>Activity: Masked customer/product projection
        Activity-->>Web: Bounded page and pagination metadata
        Web-->>Browser: Bounded page and pagination metadata
    end

    Note over Analytics,DB: Identical event IDs and search terms remain isolated by tenant database.
    Note over Activity,DB: Public activity excludes address/contact data and masks customer names.
    Note over Report,DB: Missing evidence produces an honest empty/zero metric, not an inferred conversion rate.
